---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="Privacy Policy - Luke Stahl"
	description="What lukestahl.io collects, which services see it, and how to unsubscribe or ask me to delete your data."
	canonicalUrl="https://lukestahl.io/privacy/"
	showAnnouncement={false}
	loadFontAwesome={false}
	inlineCriticalCSS={true}
>
	<main class="privacy-page">
		<article class="privacy-content">
			<p class="privacy-label">PRIVACY</p>
			<h1>Privacy policy</h1>
			<p class="privacy-updated">Last updated October 9, 2026</p>

			<p>
				lukestahl.io is a personal site. I run it, I write it, and I keep data collection small.
				This page lists what the site collects, which services handle it, and how to get in touch if you want something removed.
			</p>

			<h2>What I collect</h2>
			<ul>
				<li>
					<strong>Analytics.</strong> PostHog records page views, page leaves, performance timings, and clicks.
					Visitors who haven't identified themselves don't get a person profile. Session recordings are turned off.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Error reports.</strong> Sentry receives JavaScript errors and the page they happened on, so I can fix them. A sample of page loads is also sent for performance monitoring.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Newsletter signups.</strong> If you subscribe to The Builder, I store your email address. Nothing else is required.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Comments.</strong> Blog comments run on Giscus, which uses GitHub Discussions. If you comment, GitHub handles your sign-in and your comment is public.
				</li>
			</ul>

			<h2>Who sees it</h2>
			<ul>
				<li><strong>PostHog</strong> receives analytics events through a proxy on <code>t.lukestahl.io</code>.</li>
				<li><strong>Sentry</strong> receives error and performance data.</li>
				<li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> handles DNS for the domain.</li>
				<li><strong>GitHub</strong> hosts the site on GitHub Pages and sees standard request data such as IP address and browser.</li>
				<li><strong>Render</strong> hosts the API that stores newsletter signups.</li>
				<li><strong>Resend</strong> sends the newsletter.</li>
				<li><strong>cdnjs (Cloudflare)</strong> serves a few third-party assets, such as icon fonts, on some pages.</li>
			</ul>
			<p>I don't sell your data and I don't run ads.</p>

			<h2>Cookies and local storage</h2>
			<p>
				PostHog stores an anonymous ID in your browser so it can tell repeat visits apart. The site also remembers your light or dark mode choice in local storage.
				If you'd rather not be tracked, a browser tracking blocker will stop PostHog and Sentry. The site works without them.
			</p>

			<h2>Newsletter</h2>
			<p>
				Every issue has an unsubscribe link in the footer. Use it and you're off the list. Or email me and I'll remove you by hand.
			</p>

			<h2>Your data</h2>
			<p>
				You can ask what I have on you, ask me to delete it, or ask me to correct it. Email <a href="mailto:luke@lukestahl.io">luke@lukestahl.io</a> and I'll respond. If you're in the EU, UK, or California, you also have legal rights over your data, and the same address is how to use them.
			</p>

			<h2>Kids</h2>
			<p>This site is written for working developers and marketers. It isn't aimed at children under 13, and I don't knowingly collect their data.</p>

			<h2>Changes</h2>
			<p>If this page changes in a way that matters, I'll update the date at the top.</p>
		</article>
	</main>
</Layout>

<style>
	.privacy-page {
		max-width: 720px;
		margin: 0 auto;
		padding: 6rem 1.25rem 4rem;
		color: var(--text-primary);
	}

	.privacy-content {
		background: var(--bg-secondary);
		border: 1px solid rgba(96, 165, 250, 0.15);
		border-radius: 16px;
		box-shadow: 0 8px 32px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);
		padding: 3rem;
	}

	@media (max-width: 768px) {
		.privacy-content {
			padding: 1.75rem 1.25rem;
		}
	}

	.privacy-label {
		font-family: 'Fira Code', monospace;
		font-size: 0.75rem;
		letter-spacing: 0.15em;
		color: var(--text-secondary);
		margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
	}

	h1 {
		font-family: 'Fira Code', monospace;
		font-size: 2rem;
		margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
	}

	h2 {
		font-family: 'Fira Code', monospace;
		font-size: 1.25rem;
		margin: 2.5rem 0 0.75rem;
	}

	.privacy-updated {
		color: var(--text-secondary);
		margin: 0 0 2rem;
	}

	p,
	li {
		line-height: 1.7;
	}

	ul {
		padding-left: 1.25rem;
	}

	li {
		margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
	}

	a {
		color: var(--accent-primary);
	}
</style>
